KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ constructed stream is good: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of system-header function
--
[ostringstream.cons]/1, [basic.ios.members]: a newly constructed
ostringstream has state goodbit.  The front end converts libc++'s
basic_ostringstream without drops (cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/
test_sstream.desc), but ios_base::init, ios_base::~ios_base and locale's
constructor and destructor are defined in libc++.so and have no models ("no
body for callee"), so the stream state is nondeterministic.  A library
modelling gap, not a front-end bug.  clang++ 18 -stdlib=libc++ accepts this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
